{
  "_meta": {
    "dataset": "nepal_district_reference_points_dev_fallback",
    "description": "Approximate administrative-centre (headquarters town) coordinates for each of Nepal's 77 districts, for a single narrow purpose: a deterministic nearest-neighbour jurisdiction fallback on backends with no PostGIS point-in-polygon support (SQLite dev/test only).",
    "source_type": "general_geographic_knowledge",
    "verification_status": "approximate_reference_only",
    "contains_geometry": false,
    "notes": "These are NOT surveyed centroids and NOT district boundaries - just a single reference point per district, good enough to pick 'closest district headquarters' but not to answer 'is this point inside the district'. Never used when PostGIS is available: geolocation_service.spatial_backend_available() gates this out in any real PostgreSQL+PostGIS deployment, where the existing ST_Contains boundary-polygon lookup runs unchanged. Every response produced via this fallback is tagged reason='dev_nearest_centroid_fallback' so it can never be mistaken for a real polygon match."
  },
